From 18d914e3cc5b858306fc6635178e87f24939a50d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: microns-mcell <bartol@salk.edu>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:39:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] perf: disable the per-move intersecting-face symmetry
 assert

State::assignNewVertexCoords runs once per vertex move and asserted
Intersecting_Faces::intFacesAreSymmetric(), which traverses the whole
intersecting-faces map with a hash lookup per entry -- O(intersections)
per move. The same call inside meshmorph.cc's move loop was already
commented out, so this was the surviving copy.

The makefile does not define NDEBUG, so the assert is live in the -O3
build. It is invisible on models with few intersections and dominant on
models with many.

Measured: 1443 moves in 1741s -> 1872 moves in 1764s (0.83 -> 1.06 moves/s).
Startup state bit-identical (1502800 nonnice, 2961004 intersections).
---
 meshmorph/state.cc | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meshmorph/state.cc b/meshmorph/state.cc
index d1869a8..b4cea92 100644
--- a/meshmorph/state.cc
+++ b/meshmorph/state.cc
@@ -509,7 +509,12 @@ bool State::assignNewVertexCoords (Vertex * const v,
     v_set ps = getVertsForPartialClosestPtSearch(lower,upper);
     // update closest point and global energy 
     // for affected vertices collected before
-    assert(Intersecting_Faces::instance().intFacesAreSymmetric());
+    // DISABLED: this walks the ENTIRE intersecting-faces map and does a
+    // hash lookup per entry, on EVERY vertex move. The identical call in
+    // meshmorph.cc's move loop was already commented out for the same
+    // reason. Measured on a 5.18M-face EM model with 2.96M intersections:
+    // removing it took the move rate from 0.83/s to 1.06/s.
+    //assert(Intersecting_Faces::instance().intFacesAreSymmetric());
     Search_Stats ss = updateClosestFaceToVertices(v,fs,ps);
     // update sets with squared virtual displacement of nearby vertices
     updateVertexVD(v);
